# ============================================================================
# 📚 LEARNER GUIDE: Frontend .dockerignore — frontend/.dockerignore
# ============================================================================
# WHAT IS THIS?
# -------------
# Like root .dockerignore, but for frontend Docker build (context: ./frontend).
# Tells `docker build ./frontend` which files to EXCLUDE when copying via `COPY . .`
# in frontend/Dockerfile.
#
# WHY NEEDED?
# -----------
# - Smaller context (exclude node_modules, .next, etc. — huge!)
# - Faster build (less to send to daemon)
# - Avoid cache invalidation (if .next changes, COPY . . would invalidate)
#
# HOW IT WORKS:
# -------------
# - Each line is a pattern to ignore
# - No `!` exceptions here (simpler than root)
#
# FLOW:
# -----
# 1. docker build ./frontend → Reads frontend/.dockerignore
# 2. Excludes matching files from build context
# 3. Only non-ignored files are copied via COPY . . in Dockerfile
# ============================================================================

# Don't copy host node_modules (huge, host-specific, image will npm ci)
node_modules

# Don't copy Next.js build output (host, not for image — builder stage will rebuild)
.next

# Don't copy git (not needed in image)
.git

# Don't copy env files (contain secrets, host-specific)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Don't copy docs (not needed in image)
*.md

# Don't copy gitignore (not needed)
.gitignore

# Duplicate .next (redundant, but okay)
.next

# Don't copy npm/yarn logs (junk)
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# 💡 LEARNER TIP: Frontend vs Root .dockerignore
#   - Root .dockerignore: For `docker build .` (main Dockerfile, context: .)
#   - Frontend .dockerignore: For `docker build ./frontend` (frontend Dockerfile, context: ./frontend)
#   They are separate! Each build context has its own .dockerignore.
